{"skill":{"slug":"domain","displayName":"DomainKits - Domain Name Data and Intelligence"},"version":{"version":"3.1.4","createdAt":1790663964584,"changelog":"- Simplified and reorganized instructions for using DomainKits tools, including clear tool selection guidance by domain lifecycle stage.\n- Clarified how to report multi-page results and how to handle quota limits.\n- Added explicit direction to confirm user goals before running multi-tool sequences.\n- Updated information on integrations and access points for multiple platforms.\n- Improved privacy, account, and workflow instructions for better usability and transparency.\n- Removed the file skill-card.md.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"skill.md","size":5390,"sha256":"dccb19763bde7b435fa4bb50beb240be53c193e983fc2f01263c8ef930ab3f5c","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1846,"sha256":"893283108d7576018437a5d1940ac4630c002faaaf9ae066a4649feec7480173","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1790664363626,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2ccb0903617ee3f6faf5f1705c5147776dd6b6a69e4a44ebea89b6bcb2147198","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2ccb0903617ee3f6faf5f1705c5147776dd6b6a69e4a44ebea89b6bcb2147198","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1790664308730},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":7,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1790664363626},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill transparently connects an assistant to DomainKits for domain lookups and does not show hidden, destructive, or unrelated behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"User domain queries and optional account credentials would go to DomainKits, which is proportionate for the service but should be understood before use.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Setup registers a remote HTTP MCP endpoint with an optional API key; this is disclosed and expected for a live domain-data integration, with no local executable scripts in the artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions are scoped to selecting and reporting on domain-data tools, include quota-conscious behavior, and require user confirmation before unsolicited multi-tool sequences or account data changes.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact says memory is off by default and account-stored preferences, monitors, or strategies require explicit consent; the MCP registration itself may persist in the user's client until removed.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is live domain availability, WHOIS, DNS, pricing, trends, and related domain analysis; the listed tools and DomainKits MCP endpoint match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you are comfortable sending domain-search queries, related lookup targets, and any optional API key to DomainKits. Use account features such as preferences, monitors, or strategies only when you intentionally want DomainKits to store that data.","findings":"[E1] expected: The flagged external URL is the disclosed DomainKits MCP API endpoint needed for live domain lookups; the artifact does not show covert transmission, unrelated data collection, or local code execution.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1790664363626}}}}}